# NOTES #

^  [LINK: (a) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_ref-vp_21-0]   [LINK: (b) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_ref-vp_21-1]  These numbers are not official.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_ref-24]  The Central Committee when it convenes for its first session after being elected by a  [LINK: (National Party Congress) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Congress_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam]  elects the Politburo. [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_note-FOOTNOTEVanCooper198369-22]  According to David Koh, in interviews with several high-standing Vietnamese officials, the Politburo ranking is based upon the number of approval votes given by the Central Committee.  [LINK: (Lê Hồng Anh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%AA_H%E1%BB%93ng_Anh] , the  [LINK: (Minister of Public Security) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Public_Security_(Vietnam)] , was ranked 2nd in the  [LINK: (10th Politburo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/10th_Politburo_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam]  because he received the second-highest number of approval votes. Another example being  [LINK: (Tô Huy Rứa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%B4_Huy_R%E1%BB%A9a]  of the 10th Politburo, he was ranked at the bottom because he received the lowest number of approval votes. This system was implemented at the 1st plenum of the 10th Central Committee. [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKoh2008666-23]  Before the 10th Party Congress Politburo rankings functioned as the official  [LINK: (order of precedence) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Order_of_precedence] , but it no longer does (however, there are some who disagree with this view). [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_note-FOOTNOTEVanCooper198369-22]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_ref-tc_25-0]  He was ranked No. 1 until the  [LINK: (1945 August Revolution) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_Revolution]  led by  [LINK: (Hồ Chí Minh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ho_Chi_Minh] .

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_ref-26]  He was ranked second until the death of Hồ Chí Minh, the CPV chairman, on 2 September 1969. [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrocheux2007174-12]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam#cite_ref-29]  He is currently the only living former general secretary


